.TH WREX-DHCP6 7 "2026-10-18" "wrex 0.1.0" "wrex Manual"
.SH NAME
wrex-dhcp6 \- dhcp6 layer for \fBwrex\fR(1)

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwrex\fR \fIcraft\fR|\fIsend\fR [options] \fB--layer\fR \fIdhcp6\fR \fB--dhcp6\-<field>\fR=\fIVALUE\fR ...
\fBwrex\fR \fIfields\fR \fIdhcp6\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
DHCPv6 (RFC 8415) over UDP 546/547: the 4\-byte fixed header (msg_type 1\-13 + the 3\-byte trans_id) — everything else is options (u16 code, u16 len TLVs). Craft: \-\-dhcp6\-msg_type takes the named grammar (solicit|…|relay_reply or 1\-13; relay 12/13 crafting is deferred — a pointed write error), \-\-dhcp6\-options takes the list grammar (client_id:HEX, server_id:HEX, ia_na:IAID[,t1,t2], ia_addr:IP[,preferred,valid] — IAADDR nests inside IA_NA, oro:N…, dns:IP…, domain:NAME, elapsed:N, rapid, hex:CODE:HEX). Dissect: every option lands in the dissect\-only opt record section (opt.0.code/len/value raw + typed ip/num/text subset); IA_NA payloads render one level of sub\-options as opt.N.sub.M.* records (deeper nesting flattens into value); relay shapes (12/13) dissect their 34\-byte extended header (hop_count, link_addr, peer_addr — dissect\-only). udp dispatches ports 546/547 into this codec. Deferrals: DHCPv6 auth (option 11), relay crafting, reconfigure/keyed surfaces, DUID structured typing, CLI\-settable option records.
.

.SH ENCAPSULATION
Rank 40; stacks on udp (parents).

.SH "FIELD FLAGS"
Dots in field paths become dashes in flags (ipv4.ttl -> --ipv4-ttl, --dhcp6-msg_type).
Explicit values always win over autofill and are kept
unvalidated; \fB\-\-strict\fR re-validates (violations exit 2).
.TP
\fB\-\-dhcp6\-msg_type=\fIINT\fR\fR
message type: solicit|advertise|request|confirm|renew|rebind|reply|release|decline|reconfigure|info_req|relay_forward|relay_reply or 1\-13 (relay crafting deferred: 12/13 are pointed write errors) Type str. Default: solicit.
.TP
\fB\-\-dhcp6\-trans_id=\fIINT\fR\fR
transaction id (3 bytes on the wire; over\-wide values mask) Type u32. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-dhcp6\-options=\fIINT\fR\fR
options list grammar: client_id:HEX, server_id:HEX, ia_na:IAID[,t1,t2], ia_addr:IP[,preferred,valid], oro:N…, dns:IP…, domain:NAME, elapsed:N, rapid, hex:CODE:HEX Type str. Default: .

.SH "RECORD SECTIONS"
Repeated record sections; dissected fields carry indexed paths (opt.0.field).

.TP
\fBopt\fR (dissect\-only)
DHCPv6 option TLVs after the 4\-byte header (dissect\-only; indexed paths opt.0.code, opt.0.value, …)
  code (u16; default 0). option code (RFC 8415 §21; 3 = ia_na, 23 = dns servers)
  len (u16; default 0). option data length in bytes
  value (bytes; default ). raw option data hex (the wire truth)
  ip (ipv6; default ::). typed address: first dns server (23), IAADDR address (5)
  num (u32; default 0). typed number: first oro code (6), elapsed time (8)
  text (str; default ). typed string: domain search list (24, names joined by `,`)
.TP
\fBsub\fR (dissect\-only)
ONE level of nested sub\-options inside an IA_NA record (dissect\-only; indexed paths opt.0.sub.0.*, … — deeper nesting flattens into value)
  code (u16; default 0). sub\-option code (IA_NA payload; 5 = ia_addr)
  len (u16; default 0). sub\-option data length in bytes
  value (bytes; default ). raw sub\-option data hex (the wire truth)
  ip (ipv6; default ::). typed IAADDR address (sub\-option 5)
  preferred (u32; default 0). typed IAADDR preferred lifetime (sub\-option 5)
  valid (u32; default 0). typed IAADDR valid lifetime (sub\-option 5)

.SH EXAMPLES
wrex fields dhcp6

